ROS 2 Optimization Notes for Raspberry Pi Nodes
Based on our successful fusion node optimization, here are key insights to share with other chats for optimizing ROS 2 nodes on Raspberry Pi:
System Context

Resource Constraints

Raspberry Pi has limited CPU and memory
Multiple nodes compete for the same resources (YOLO ~30%, LiDAR ~20%, etc.)
Overloaded nodes can cause system-wide performance degradation


Common Issues to Look For

High CPU usage (>50% for a single node is problematic)
Frequent memory allocations/deallocations
Excessive logging
Redundant calculations
Inefficient transforms and sensor processing



Key Optimization Strategies
1. Memory Management

Use fixed-size buffers with pre-allocation instead of growing collections
Reuse objects instead of creating new ones each time
Minimize deep copies of large data structures
Consider using NumPy arrays with explicit data types (np.float32)

2. Computational Efficiency

Identify and optimize hot paths in the code
Cache calculations that are used repeatedly
Use appropriate data structures for frequent operations
Consider downsampling data when full resolution isn't needed

3. Timer and Callback Management

Reduce timer frequencies to minimum necessary
Use callback groups to manage concurrency
Implement staged startup to avoid CPU spikes
Prioritize critical processing over less important tasks

4. Transform Optimization

Cache transforms that don't change frequently
Batch transform operations when possible
Consider using simplified transform calculations for performance-critical paths

5. Sensor Data Processing

Implement clear sensor priority systems
Process high-quality sensors first, fall back to others when needed
Filter redundant or noisy sensor data early
Use adaptive processing rates based on activity level

6. Logging Optimization

Implement throttled logging with configurable intervals
Use different log levels appropriately
Include timestamps that can correlate with other system logs
Consider periodic summary logs instead of continuous updates

Code Architecture Improvements

Dedicated Classes

Separate concerns into focused classes (e.g., MotionStateManager, SensorManager)
Clear interfaces between components
Explicit state management with proper encapsulation


Algorithm Refinements

Balance responsiveness vs. stability with appropriate hysteresis
Use consistent validation thresholds with context-awareness
Implement physics-based constraints appropriate to the domain
Consider computational cost of advanced algorithms


Fault Tolerance

Add defensive checking for attribute existence
Type conversion for serialization (NumPy types to Python types)
Graceful degradation when sensors fail
Appropriate recovery mechanisms



Implementation Tips

Profile Before Optimizing

Identify the actual bottlenecks rather than guessing
Focus on the 20% of code that uses 80% of resources
Measure the impact of changes


ROS 2-Specific Optimizations

Use appropriate QoS settings for different types of data
Consider message pooling for high-frequency topics
Leverage lifecycle management for resource coordination
Use efficient message types (avoid String for binary data)


Raspberry Pi Considerations

Be mindful of I/O operations (disk, network)
Monitor temperature to avoid thermal throttling
Consider process priorities for critical nodes
Be aware of differences between Pi 4 and Pi 5 capabilities



